<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vikramarjuna Vijaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">941</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Pampa Bharata</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vikramarjuna Vijaya, also called the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adikavi-pampa">Pampa</a> Bharata, is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannada">Kannada</a> epic by the poet Pampa, completed around 941. A retelling of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a> centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arjuna">Arjuna</a>, it identifies the hero with Pampa's patron, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vemulawada">Vemulavada</a> Chalukya king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arikesari-ii">Arikesari II</a>. With Pampa's Adipurana it is regarded as a foundation of classical Kannada literature.</p></div>
